saf=[[
      == w a r n i n g ==

       health and safety

    this videogame could be

   identified to potentially

  trigger seizures for people

 with photosensitive epilepsy.

 viewer discretion is advised.
]]

cop=[[
    == c o p y r i g h t ==

this program is worthware. if
you like it, you are encouraged
to pay what you think it is
worth to you on select gaming
sites.

this funding will go towards
writing future turn-based
thinking games.

if you use any media or source
from this program for your own
projects, please give credit to the
the author for their dilligent
effort. thank you.
]]

inx=[[
    m i l d e w - m a n o r

   written by dw817 (david w)

http://www.writerscafe.org/dw817

   ----- (c) aug 2018+ ------

    press Ž for high scores
    hold — to speed-up text




old man mildew, a tycoon and
billionaire had recently died,
and according to his will, had
left nothing at all for his
relatives.

enraged with these events, they
vowed to tear apart his manor,
seeking the treasures he had
apparently hidden within.

but the spirit of mildew was
outraged and angered by this.

rising from the grave, he
returned back to his home. once
there he apparently did away
with all those living who had
sought after his immense
fortune.

2-days later, you step into the
scene. an investigator by trade.
you are offered one-million
dollars in cash from the last
surviving relative. all you need
to do is find out what happened
to the others by entering the
manor.

on the very day of halloween at
11pm, you enter within the
premises. at once you can tell
there is no electricity - and
no illumination at all for that
matter.

but you came prepared. you are
wearing a special armor that
has a forcefield charge of 9 to
protect you from dangers.

you also have in your pack a
trusty hurricane lamp and some
matches in your pocket to light
it.

chuckling at the darkness, you
reach in your pack to pull the
lamp out when suddenly, some
unseen force wrenches it from
your grip and - horrors - dashes
it to the stone floor where it
smashes in pieces!

there is a gust of cold air
around you and the door behind
you clicks locked and closed.

then you are greeted to a deep
and evil chuckling.

it's the spirit of old man
mildew himself! he speaks:

"welcome traveler. i suppose
 you have come to try and steal
 my fortune - just like the
 the other idiots before you.
 and you will meet your fate -
 just like them!"
 
fearfully, you yell back a
reply, "i'm only looking for - "

but mildew cuts you off.
"worry not traveler. your life
 is not forfeit, not yet! for
 i enjoy games and i have one
 for you. find the others if
 you can, but never touch the
 walls! never!"

"to make it interesting, i
 give you one hour's time to
 find the other 12. but after
 that time, halloween midnight,
 you had better be out of my
 sight and home - or i will
 deal with you myself -
 personally!"

with that it grows silent and
quiet around you. just then a
bolt of lightning flickers
outside, and for that brief
moment - you can see around you
- if just for a little bit.
 
you still have your matches too.
they can provide some better
illumination. press Ž to use
one of them.

if you find any keys, they can
be used with —.

so this is how it will be. you
can navigate throughout this
haunted house - whenever the
lightning flashes or you can
strike up a match.

you are also armed with a
compass to find hidden items
and a meter to locate invisible
ghosts.

that and you are only given a
single hour in which to find
the 12 others.

but for a million dollars, you
can put up with this - and vow
to accomplish your mission
within the time limit that 
mildew has issued you ...

be ready traveler, for your
adventure begins now!

. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .

    press [z] key to begin
. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
]]

